## Indexing Files From Different Locations

### Scenario 1 — File is on THIS machine (where Cursor is running)
When user says "index this file/folder from my machine / local machine / this laptop":
1. Call `prepare_cursor_machine_upload(source_name="chosen-name")` to get the SCP command and staging path
2. Show the returned `scp_command` to the user with LOCAL_PATH replaced by their actual path
3. Run the `scp_command` in the LOCAL terminal (this sends files to the server)
4. Call `index_local_path(local_path=<staging_path>, source_name="chosen-name")`

### Scenario 2 — File is on a REMOTE system (not this machine, not the server)
When user says "index files from server X / machine at IP / another system":
- If credentials already saved: `index_remote_path(remote_path="...", source_name="...", system_name="saved-name")`
- If new system with inline creds: `index_remote_path(remote_path="...", source_name="...", host="IP", user="user", ssh_key="/root/.ssh/id_rsa", save_credentials=true, system_name="new-name")`
  - `save_credentials=true` saves them to remote_systems.json on the server for future use
- The server SSHes into the remote machine, SCPs the files, indexes them

### Scenario 3 — File is already on the SERVER
`index_local_path(local_path="/absolute/path/on/server", source_name="chosen-name")`

