## Python Package → Indexed Repo Mapping

When you see a Python import, map it to the correct indexed repo name using this table.
Always pass the `repo_name` filter when searching to avoid noise from other repos.

| Python import prefix | Indexed repo name |
|---|---|
| `sundancemesa` / `sundancemesa.*` | `frameworks.validation.pythonsv.projects.sundancemesa` |
| `common_utils` / `common_utils.*` | `applications.validation.fpga.solutions.utilities.utilities` |

### Usage rule
When the user references or imports anything from `sundancemesa`:
1. Use `search_repository_code(query="...", repo_name="frameworks.validation.pythonsv.projects.sundancemesa")`
2. Use `get_repository_file(repo_name="frameworks.validation.pythonsv.projects.sundancemesa", path="...")`
3. Do NOT search all repos — always scope to the mapped repo name above

When the user references or imports anything from `common_utils`:
1. Use `search_repository_code(query="...", repo_name="applications.validation.fpga.solutions.utilities.utilities")`
2. Use `get_repository_file(repo_name="applications.validation.fpga.solutions.utilities.utilities", path="...")`
3. Do NOT search all repos — always scope to the mapped repo name above

### Example
```python
from sundancemesa.network.eth.eth_vsip_frame_buf import VSIPFrameBuffer
```
→ search `repo_name="frameworks.validation.pythonsv.projects.sundancemesa"` for `VSIPFrameBuffer` or `eth_vsip_frame_buf`

```python
from common_utils import some_helper
import common_utils
```
→ search `repo_name="applications.validation.fpga.solutions.utilities.utilities"` for `some_helper` or relevant symbol
